    "updated_at": "2020-11-18T13:40:31Z",
    "body": "I'm thinking a solution to this would have to include some JavaScript, something along the lines of `requestFullscreen`. (`Element.requestTopLayer()` or `Element.requestStackingParent(otherElement)`) ?. \r\n\r\nTrying to solve it in pure-CSS, considering the stacking context \"contract\" between the element's children and an element's surrounding may end up being over-complicated.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
